# vehje-check. Design

The framework's graded check pass. The crate directory is `vehje-typecheck` and
plays the `vehje-check` role; the rename of the directory to `vehje-check` is
deferred to a later round (moving the doc templates during a source phase trips
the doc-phase gate), so these docs describe the role under the `vehje-check`
name while the directory keeps its current name. It discharges the graded
(co)modal judgment over the resolved Core IR: it infers the effect, lease, and
binding-time grades, checks inclusion against a target's declaration, computes
assurance, and mints the checked witness. Like resolve it is framework-owned,
because the shared passes are what make the shared IR real rather than nominal.
`#![no_std]`, no alloc.

The pass is where the type-system-as-verification identity lives. The three
static proof axes plus assurance are one graded judgment, not four analyses,
and they discharge here during a bottom-up fold, reusing one bitmask machinery.
The reachability and lease inference and the effect inference are fixpoint
queries on `vehje-fixpoint`; the per-family axiom table and the lease-rule
schema come from `vehje-signature`.

## The graded judgment

- `check`. The entry: it runs the graded inference over the resolved IR (using
  the `Resolution` side-table from `vehje-resolve`), writes the grade
  annotations into `vehje-ir`'s `GradeTable`, and returns a `Graded` witness on a
  clean fold or a `CheckError`. `Graded` is the evidence-of-check the mint
  requires, so the witness cannot be minted without a clean check having run;
  this is the DESIGN's "check mints the witness" contract made unskippable across
  the check/mint split.
- Effect inference. The effect axis is a graded monad. The pass infers each
  construct's effect set (the operations it invokes that are not locally
  handled) as a thermometer-encoded bottom-up bitmask join, so the lattice join
  is a bitwise OR and the inclusion check against a target's `Permits` is a
  subset test (both benched negligible). A locally handled operation drops out
  of the residual's effect the way a reduced build-environment effect did.
- Lease and reachability inference. The lease axis is a coeffect whose grade is
  a reachability qualifier. The pass computes the reach-mask for each value as a
  fixpoint query: the naming set is bounded by the reachability-type binder rule
  (at `Let` and `Lambda`, splice the bound expression's reach set where the body
  reaches the variable, then drop the variable), and the escape set by region
  promotion. The immutable strictly-nested depth-lease is the degenerate
  qualifier that ships first; the full qualifier lattice is deferred. The
  effect-coeffect interaction is graded def-use, so the link-or-consume bit is a
  monotone function of the operand's declared effect, read from the
  `vehje-signature` lease-rule schema.
- Binding-time discharge. Each property discharges at the earliest binding time
  its inputs are known: an all-early-bound property folds to a compile error, a
  late-bound one is a bounded dynamic residual. This is the extraction objective
  the lower stage reads.
- Assurance grading. A property's `Assurance` grade is a projection of its
  binding-time grade crossed with the property, so the guarantee inventory is a
  computed grade vector, not a hand-curated list.
- `Checked`. The typestate witness (moved here from the output crate): a program
  proven inclusion- and effect-checked against a specific target. Its
  constructor is crate-private, and the one sanctioned mint (`mint_checked`,
  which `vehje-codegen`'s `check_for` wraps) requires the `Graded` evidence from
  `check` and derives the target's `Supports`/`Permits` from `T: TargetSets`
  rather than from free parameters, so a caller can neither skip the check nor
  claim a support set the target does not declare. It is consumed by
  `vehje-codegen`'s `emit`, so the obligation to check is compile-time
  unskippable. Deriving the program's own used family and effect sets from the
  program (rather than trusting caller-supplied sets) is the remaining inclusion
  step, carried by the runtime-bitmask path.
- `CheckError`. Diagnostics carrying the construct and the rule violated (an
  effect outside `Permits`, a lease that cannot be placed, a family outside
  `Supports`).

## Operations, escape, and the first axis interaction

State: intended.

**The effect scope chain.** A lexically handled `Perform` contributes nothing to
the effect mask in the first place, so the mask is only ever populated by
operations that genuinely escape, which are the declared named effects a target's
`Permits` set is about. The alternative, subtracting a mask at the `Handle`, is
unsound when two operations share a slot; carrying the handled operations down
the walk as a scope chain, the way resolve already carries binders, avoids the
question rather than answering it. This retires the standing subtraction FIXME.

**The escape rule is an axis interaction, not a scoping rule.** `Perform` is not
a value, so a direct escape is impossible by construction. The residual case is a
`Lambda` whose body performs, returned out of the `Handle` and called afterward.
The effect axis records that the lambda's body performs; the coeffect axis has to
record that the lambda value can perform later. So the rule has two halves: a
promotion at `Lambda`, where the body's unhandled operations become the lambda
value's reach of the corresponding handler slots, which is the latent effect on
the arrow; and a check at `Handle`, where the result's reach must not contain the
handler's slot.

This is the first genuine effect-and-lease interaction rule in the system, which
is what the graded spine owes before the word theorem is earned. It is intended,
not proven, and it is where that debt starts being paid rather than where it is
discharged.

**Two declared error variants become real.** `ForbiddenEffect` is constructed by
the obligation that every performed operation resolves to a lexically enclosing
clause or to an operation the target permits, which is what lets the runtime
treat an unwind reaching the root as an invariant violation rather than a program
outcome. `UnplaceableLease` is constructed by the escape check above.

**The slot collision is conservative in the right direction.** Folding a node
index modulo the mask width makes two handlers share a slot, which
over-approximates reach, which produces a false refusal and never a false
acceptance. So the mechanism lands before the mask widens, and widening is an
accuracy fix rather than a soundness fix.

## Generative freshness

Generative discharge is fresh by construction. Macro expansion produces fresh
binders so capture is structurally impossible, because resolution runs after
expansion, and multi-shot resumption produces fresh continuation state per
resume so one resumption cannot corrupt another. Hygiene and multi-shot-frame
freshness are one discipline (generative freshness) seen at two binding times:
generation is fresh by construction and bounded by a host-lent budget, and
budget exhaustion is a named diagnostic distinct from a completed expansion or a
completed resumption. This is "illegal states unrepresentable" applied to
generation. State: the enforcement, and the red capturing-macro test that pins
it, are owed; the effect-subtraction obligation for a handled operation under
multi-shot resumption (a body performing a second effect) is the paired
soundness question the check must answer, refuse, or define replay semantics for.

## The validated-data slice

The pass owns the analyzer validated-data slice: the relation schemas and the
lease-rule schema the shipped runtime's analyzer stage is specialised from. The
Rust crate is the definition; the Zig analyzer is the specialised execution.

## Family-extension hooks

A family's own checks (a language's coherence rules, a document family's block
nesting rules) extend the walk through the family-extension hooks; the Core pass
runs the shared graded inference and dispatches to the family checks for family
nodes. The base pass descends into a `Raw` node's payload, joining its
children's grades exactly as it joins an `Apply`'s, rather than treating `Raw`
as a leaf.

- `FamilyCheck`. The family-extension hook trait a consumer implements to
  declare a family operation's own effect. Its `effect_of_raw` method defaults
  to the empty effect; the check pass joins the returned effect into the `Raw`
  node's grade on top of the children's. `check` is the Core-only entry (default
  hook); `check_with` takes a consumer hook.

## Non-scope

- Any one consumer's type system as surface features; those are a family's
  checks, plugged in through the hooks, not Core.
- Resolution (`vehje-resolve`), lowering (`vehje-lower`), scheduling
  (`vehje-schedule`), emission (`vehje-codegen`).
- The relational engine itself (`vehje-fixpoint`); this crate defines the
  relation schemas and runs the queries.

## Dependencies

`vehje-ir` for the IR, the grade types, and the `GradeTable`; `vehje-resolve`
for the `Resolution` side-table; `vehje-fixpoint` for the fixpoint inference;
`vehje-signature` for the lease-rule schema and per-family axiom table;
`arvo-bitmask` for the grade masks; `notko` for `Maybe` and `Outcome`.
`#![no_std]`, no alloc.
